# Pakistan History: Early Period (1947-1958) — Structured Notes

---

## Part 1: Foundational Crises (1947-1951)

### A. Birth Amidst Chaos (1947)

| Challenge | Details |
|-----------|---------|
| **Administrative Void** | Karachi built as capital from scratch; severe civil service shortage as Hindu officers left for India |
| **Radcliffe Line** | Hasty partition divided communities, irrigation, railways; 10-15M displaced; hundreds of thousands killed |
| **Uneven Asset Distribution** | ⅓ of British Indian Army; ₹75 crore withheld by India (released after Gandhi's intervention) |
| **Interim Constitution** | Adapted 1935 Act — inadequate for sovereignty, creating governance ambiguity |
| **Kashmir Crisis** | Muslim-majority state; Hindu ruler acceded to India (Oct 1947) after tribal invasion; first Indo-Pak war (1947-48); UN ceasefire (1949) established LoC — permanent national wound |

---

### B. Leadership Vacuum (1948-1951)

**September 11, 1948** — **Jinnah's death** from undisclosed tuberculosis/lung cancer removed sole unifying figure

**Khawaja Nazimuddin** succeeded as Governor-General — politically weak

**Liaquat Ali Khan** (Prime Minister):
- Stabilized economy, refugees, constitutional work
- **Objectives Resolution (1949)** — philosophical foundation for all future constitutions
- US visit (1950) — early Cold War alignment

**October 16, 1951** — **Liaquat assassinated** in Rawalpindi; unsolved mystery (suspects: US, Afghanistan, Iran, domestic rivals); death opened era of instability

